Make sdcdb usable against SDCC 4.5.0 .cdb output + the bundled uCsim 0.8.15.

Three independent defects, all of which stop sdcdb cold for this target:

1. readCdb() stores each .cdb record line verbatim, including the trailing
   newline fgets() leaves on it. For an "M:<module>" record the module name
   then becomes "<module>\n", so the source file is looked up as
   "<module>\n.c" and never found -- every module fails to load.

2. searchDirsFname()'s '_'->'.' fallback never advances past the underscore
   it just restored, so strchr() re-finds the same '_' on the next iteration
   and the function spins forever. Only reachable when a source file is
   missing AND its module name contains '_' (bb_spi, rf_controller,
   user_matrix, ...) -- exactly what bug #1 induces, so sdcdb hangs at startup.

3. openSimulator() puts the command socket in non-blocking mode, but
   waitForSim() frames a reply by reading until uCsim's '\0' prompt. On a
   non-blocking socket the read returns on the first EAGAIN -- typically
   before the reply lands -- so the stop address parses as 0 and every
   'run'/'step' is reported as halting at 0x0000. Keep the socket blocking so
   the read waits for the terminating prompt.

--- a/debugger/mcs51/sdcdb.c
+++ b/debugger/mcs51/sdcdb.c
@@ -414,6 +414,13 @@
             }
 
           bp += 2;
+          {
+            /* fgets keeps the trailing newline; strip it so module names
+               (and every other record) are not terminated by '\n'. */
+            size_t _blen = strlen(bp);
+            while (_blen && (bp[_blen-1] == '\n' || bp[_blen-1] == '\r'))
+              bp[--_blen] = '\0';
+          }
           currl->line = Safe_malloc(strlen(bp)+1);
           strcpy(currl->line, bp);
         }
@@ -485,6 +492,7 @@
           if (NULL != (found = searchDirsFname(fname)))
             return found;
           *p = '_'; // not found, restore '_' and try next '_'
+          p++;      // advance past it, else strchr re-finds the same '_'
         }
     }
   return NULL;
